{"id":"big-ben","name":"Big Ben","qid":"Q41225","country":"United Kingdom","locality":"City of Westminster","lat":"51.50067","lon":"-0.12457","built":"1843","year":1843,"year_text":"1843","century":"19th century","era":"19th century","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Gothic Revival","heritage":"","type":"bell; clock tower; national symbol; steeple; striking clock; clock bell; architectural element; cultural icon; inclined tower; belfry","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Ben","text":"Big Ben is the nickname for the Great Bell of the Great Clock of Westminster, and, by extension, for the clock tower that stands at the north end of the Palace of Westminster in London, England. Originally named the Clock Tower, the structure was renamed the Elizabeth Tower in 2012 to mark the Diamond Jubilee of Queen Elizabeth II. The clock is a striking clock with five bells.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Ben","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-4015996bc04d","w":691,"h":1200,"title":"Big Ben, Londres, Inglaterra, 2014-08-11, DD 200.JPG","o":"gh-4015996bc04d.jpg","credit":{"text":"Diego Delso","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Big_Ben%2C_Londres%2C_Inglaterra%2C_2014-08-11%2C_DD_200.JPG","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-a140cb769c9f","w":675,"h":1200,"title":"Elizabeth Tower and the north front of the Palace of Westminster, London.jpg","o":"gh-a140cb769c9f.jpg","credit":{"text":"Christian David","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elizabeth_Tower_and_the_north_front_of_the_Palace_of_Westminster%2C_London.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-b32d3118d9fa","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Rear of Big Ben clock face.jpg","o":"gh-b32d3118d9fa.jpg","credit":{"text":"Sergeant Adrian Harlen","license":"OGL 3","license_ur